## Choose the owner

| Content                                  | Owner                  |
| ---------------------------------------- | ---------------------- |
| Purpose and first command                | Root `README.md`       |
| Documentation navigation                 | `docs/README.md`       |
| Architecture and dependency direction    | `docs/architecture.md` |
| Setup, checks and local tooling           | `docs/development.md`  |
| Unfinished work                           | `ROADMAP.md`           |

## Structure docs as a small book

The root README is the cover. `docs/README.md` is the index. Every page below it
starts with a `Parent:` link. Pages with multiple main sections include a linked
table of contents.

## Describe the present

Unmarked prose describes implemented behavior. Put unfinished behavior in the
roadmap instead of presenting it as current.

## Review checklist

- The page answers one reader question.
- No other page owns the same fact.
- Parent and local links resolve.
- The page is reachable from the root README.
- Future work stays in the roadmap.
